    12	specialization inequality, and normalized cubic-resolvent construction.  Its
    13	corrections strengthen the usable theorem:
    14	
    15	> For every actual rank-four proper block, the reduced target branch `B` has
    16	> `b1(B)>=1`; hence there is at least one `(2,2)` fibre.  After binding Chau's
    17	> published polynomial-parametrization theorem as done below, the full
