   582	## 11. Maximum-safe theorem
   583	
   584	Everything below is proved, not conjectured.
   585	
   586	**Theorem (safe form, strictly stronger than the charged (0.3)).**
   587	Let `B ⊂ A^2` be a reduced irreducible affine plane curve with
   588	
   589	```text
   590	(H1) exactly one place at infinity (equivalently, B is connected at
   591	     infinity, equivalently its link at infinity K is a knot);
   592	(H2) gamma + delta = 1, where gamma is the geometric genus of B and
   593	     delta = sum of the delta invariants of its affine singularities.
   594	```
   595	
   596	Let `rho: pi1(A^2 - B) -> S_d` send generic meridians to transpositions with
   597	transitive image. Then `d <= 3`.
   598	
   599	The charged theorem is the sub-case `gamma = 0`, `delta = 1`, singularity an
   600	ordinary node. The extension is free: (H1) plus reducedness is all that
   601	Lemma 7.1 needs, and the genus law below replaces the node-specific Euler
   602	count.
   603	
   604	**(R1) Genus law.** Under (H1) and goodness, `g_3(K) = gamma + delta`.
   605	Proof: `chi(F_eps) = chi(B) - sum mu_p`, `chi(B) = (1 - 2 gamma) - sum(r_p - 1)`,
   606	`mu_p = 2 delta_p - r_p + 1`, so `chi(F_eps) = 1 - 2 gamma - 2 delta`;
   607	`F_eps` has one end, so `g(F_eps) = gamma + delta`; by Neumann 1989
   608	Theorem 1 that core is a minimal Seifert surface for `K`. This reproduces
   609	`g = 1` for the charged case and is the invariant form of the report's
   610	Section 2 count.
   611	
   612	**(R2) Degree law.** `d <= 1 + mr(K) <= 1 + bridge(K)`, where `mr` is the
   613	meridional rank. Proof: the image is generated by `mr(K)` transpositions;
   614	the orbits of a group generated by transpositions are the components of the
   615	graph whose edges are their supports; transitivity forces that graph
   616	connected on `d` vertices, hence at least `d - 1` edges. `mr <= bridge`
   617	since a bridge presentation supplies that many meridian generators. No
   618	meridional rank conjecture is invoked, only the trivial inequality.
   619	
   620	**(R3) Sharpness at `gamma + delta = 1`.** The bound `d <= 3` cannot be
   621	improved in the safe class: the cuspidal cubic `y^2 = x^3` satisfies (H1)
   622	and (H2) with `gamma = 0`, `delta = 1`, is the discriminant of the versal
   623	deformation of `A2`, has `pi1(A^2 - B) = B_3 = <a,b | aba = bab>`, and its
   624	degree-three simple cover `{(x,p,q) : x^3 + px + q = 0}` realises a
   625	transitive transposition image in `S_3`. Within the *node* class the bound
   626	is not known to be sharp; the nodal cubic itself only reaches `d = 2`
   627	(Section 9).
   628	
   629	**Robustness.** (0.3) does not need `g_3 = 1`; `g_3 <= 1` suffices, because
   630	the extra candidate admitted, the unknot, gives `d <= 2`. So the theorem
   631	survives even if only clause (a) of Neumann Theorem 1 is granted.
   632	
   633	**What remains outside.** All five scope items of the report's Section 5
   634	stand, with item 2 sharpened: a *unibranch* singularity is not by itself
   635	outside the safe theorem (a cusp has `delta = 1` and is covered); what is
   636	outside is any configuration with `gamma + delta >= 2`. Multiple places at
   637	infinity remain the expensive horn, because Lemma 7.1 then gives nothing
   638	and goodness has to be bought separately.
   639	
   640	## 12. Corrections
   641	
   642	```text
   643	C1  Sec.4, "Both are transpositions in S_d" is asserted without the
   644	    conjugacy of meridians.  Insert: all meridians of a knot are conjugate
   645	    in its group, so the Wirtinger meridians a,b of K_infinity are
   646	    conjugate to the fibre meridians x_j, whose images are transpositions
   647	    by (0.2).
   648	    Blast radius: Sec.4 only.  Conclusion unaffected.  Severity: editorial.
   649	
   650	C2  Sec.2, formula (2.4) drops the hypotheses "p >= 2, gcd(p,q) = 1" that
   651	    the predecessor's (5.5) carries.  Without them the census argument does
   652	    not close (p = 1 returns the companion).
   653	    Blast radius: Sec.2 statement only.  Severity: editorial.
   654	
   655	C3  Sec.3 leans on "generic finite projection" to deliver both the
   656	    Zariski--van Kampen presentation and K_infinity = closure(beta_infinity).
   657	    The operative content is properness of the projection on B (leading
   658	    y-coefficient constant, no vertical asymptote) and N = deg_y f, not
   659	    N = deg f.  Worth making explicit: the wrong strand count changes the
   660	    predicted genus (Section 6.1).
   661	    Blast radius: Sec.3 exposition.  Severity: editorial.
   662	
   663	C4  Sec.2 claims g_3(K_infinity) = 1 via the "unique minimal" clause of
   664	    Neumann Theorem 1.  Only g_3 <= 1 is load-bearing, and the unknot case
   665	    it admits yields d <= 2.  The report is therefore weaker than its own
   666	    argument.  Also, Neumann's footnote 5 restricts the uniqueness to
   667	    isotopy in S^3 not fixing L; immaterial here.
   668	    Blast radius: none; the correction strengthens the result.
   669	```
