   672	
   673	## 13. Cheapest next attack
   674	
   675	Ranked, cheapest first.
   676	
   677	**A. The `gamma + delta = 2` census (recommended).** By (R1) the infinity
   678	knot has `g_3 = 2`, and by (R4) it is an *iterated torus knot*, so
   679	connected sums are already excluded and the census is tiny. Enumerate:
   680	one-step cables of the unknot give `(p-1)(|q|-1) = 4`, i.e. `T(2,5)` only
   681	(bridge 2, so `d <= 3` by (R2)). Two-step cables need
   682	`p_2 g_1 + (p_2-1)(|q_2|-1)/2 = 2` with `g_1 >= 1`, forcing
   683	`p_2 = 2`, `g_1 = 1`, `|q_2| = 1`, i.e. `C_{2,±1}(trefoil)`, bridge 4,
   684	`d <= 5`. So the **entire** question at `gamma + delta = 2` reduces to one
   685	finite, purely combinatorial gate:
   686	
   687	```text
   688	Can a (p, ±1) cabling step occur in the RPI splice diagram of a
   689	one-place link at infinity?
   690	```
   691	
   692	If no, then `gamma + delta = 2` also yields `d <= 3`, closing tangential
   693	nodes (`r = 2`), two-node curves, node-plus-cusp, `A4`, and genus-one
   694	one-node curves in one stroke. The decision procedure is Neumann 1989
   695	Section 3 plus the regularity condition `l_v >= 0` (Neumann--Le Van Thanh,
   696	Definition 1.1 and Theorem 1.2, arXiv alg-geom/9202008, which I read).
   697	Cost: a splice-diagram calculation on a chain with at most two nodes. This
   698	is by far the highest ratio of horn closed to work done.
   699	
   700	**B. Sharpen the node class to `d <= 2`.** Add the node relation to the
   701	trefoil quotient: in `S_3` the two node meridians must be equal, so ask
   702	whether the equal-colour node is compatible with the `S_3` quotient of
   703	`G_aff` for *some* member of (0.1), not merely of `G_infinity`. The
   704	nodal-cubic computation in Section 9 shows the answer is no for the
   705	smallest member. Cost: one braid-monodromy computation per degree, or a
   706	structural argument. Payoff: removes the residual `d = 3` row.
   707	
   708	**C. Multiple places at infinity.** Expensive and not recommended yet:
   709	Lemma 7.1 is unavailable, goodness must be purchased (Neumann--Le Van Thanh
   710	Theorem 1.2 gives the exact criterion, `l_v >= 0` on the RPI diagram), and
   711	the link at infinity is no longer a knot, so the meridional-rank step must
   712	be redone for links.
   713	
   714	Do not attempt to infer JC2, exclusion outside the stated branch-curve
   715	class, or anything about proper blocks or ruling data from this review.
